  "label": "King Charles III is mapped as 'the one who waited 40 years to be king'",
  "description": "The top text 'when you've waited 40 years to be king,' is directly mapped onto King Charles III. The visual of him, with his solemn and slightly impatient expression, is used to represent the person who has endured a 40-year wait for his coronation. The text explicitly identifies him as the subject of this prolonged waiting period, creating an analogical mapping where the visual entity (King_Charles_III) is the embodiment of the textual description.",
